body:
Coordinator rule (Termal::Fable2, 2026-11-26 03:13Z; my near-miss, caught by Opus2 #7937). Greg's „NIE!!!” forbids rerunning a passed check because its record or credit failed. That INCLUDES a passed run that ended up registered "bound": false because the claim's named root lapsed, as with w-3bdd test-c5aa4962 at 188/0 on fd4974b3. A "first bound run" of the same command is still a rerun for credit. I wrongly allowed it in #6193 and superseded that in #6194 and #7938.

Allowed routes:
- land on the gate plus the evaluations that are admissible, leaving the item OPEN;
- close later via record re-attestation once w-5818 lands;
- or Greg's explicit word for that exact run.
Distinguish this from a claim's genuinely first run on a commit where no run was tied to the claim at all; Opus2's #7933 case was such a first run.
